  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Founded in 1983, Club Canin de Grasse (CC06), based on chemin de Roquevignon, has a synthetic-turf agility ground and also offers hoopers (synthetic turf), obedience, tracking and clicker training.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The club has its own official website (cc06.net) and an active Facebook page, with independent confirmation via agility competition results referencing the club (briards-fr.com). A free trial session is offered to newcomers. One point to flag: two independent directories (sports-canins.net, telephone.city/mappy) link a different phone number (04 93 36 50 42) to this same address than the one published until now — it may be a manager's personal number rather than the main line, worth checking before calling.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: take advantage of the free trial session to see if agility suits your dog before committing.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The historic centre of Grasse, the world capital of perfume, is an easy visit from the club.</p>
